2. Background and Motivation

Traditional spacecraft autonomy focuses on:
   •   Predefined command sequences
   •   Limited onboard decision logic
   •   Ground-controlled mission adjustments

Emerging research in neuromorphic computing, photonic processing, and adaptive AI enables new architectures capable of:
   •   Real-time perception and decision support
   •   Event-driven processing efficiency
   •   Adaptive mission planning
   •   Autonomous system management

Q-HISS integrates these developments into a unified spacecraft intelligence framework.

